  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "The digit-sum of \\(998\\) is \\(9 + 9 + 8 = 26.\\) How many \\(3\\)-digit whole numbers, whose digit-sum is \\(26\\), are even?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\)",
    "E": "\\(5\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "An even whole number has an even units digit, so that digit is at most \\(8\\). The hundreds and tens digits are each at most \\(9\\). Thus the largest possible digit-sum of a three-digit even number is\n\\[\n9+9+8=26.\n\\]\nTo reach 26, all three digits must reach these bounds: making any digit smaller would make the sum less than 26. This forces the number to be \\(998\\).\n\nSince \\(998\\) satisfies every condition, there is exactly \\(\\boxed{1}\\) such number, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
